<article class="env-definition" id="07IX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07IX">Definition <span data-tag="07IX">60.12.1</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/07MF" data-tag="07MF">60.7.5</a> let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_{X/S}$-modules on $\text{Cris}(X/S)$. An <em>$S$-derivation $D : \mathcal{O}_{X/S} \to \mathcal{F}$</em> is a map of sheaves such that for every object $(U, T, \delta )$ of $\text{Cris}(X/S)$ the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  D : \Gamma (T, \mathcal{O}_ T) \longrightarrow \Gamma (T, \mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
  <p> is a divided power $\Gamma (V, \mathcal{O}_ V)$-derivation where $V \subset S$ is any open such that $T \to S$ factors through $V$. </p>
</article>